{"seq":14,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/qm-pi-haiku-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T00:22:22.536Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"6e6ef6aa7eab5e12b4fca1520bc4e9a3183f7f78431789e2b06568b0837cb8d4","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"#coastal-team","text":"@Bettina Kroll, here's the list for Kwame's review. Pellow Home Living is excluded.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL)**\n- Ticket #4419 (open): `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length.\n- Gate 4 chassis pool validation during shift change: noted in Moss's Coastal cheat sheet as the main friction point. No ticket number is recorded there.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF)**\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges, requested by warehouse managers.\n- Tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B. Engineering provided a manual CSV patch for the night dispatcher. No ticket number is recorded.\n\nSources: #coastal-team, #coastal-random, and Moss's Coastal cheat sheet. The `members/moss/notes` folder in the shared files is empty to me, so I used the cheat sheet in the knowledge brain. Two items I left out: ticket #8812 and the Door 4B scanner issue, which were about Covey & Lark / Pellow, and PD-8841 (Gate 4B chassis holds), which is in a 2025 wiki recap rather than the Coastal channels or notes.","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"}}
